      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First off, you should clean the wound thoroughly with soap and water, then apply a generous amount of hydrogen peroxide. You can also use a saline solution if you prefer. After that, apply a band-aid and keep it dry. If the bleeding stops and there's no severe pain, you can probably manage it yourself. But if you notice any signs of infection, like redness, swelling, or pus, then you should definitely see a doctor. Remember, I'm here to help you, but I can't replace professional medical advice.",
