      "content": "Scrubbing the wound is a good start, but you really need to clean it with soap and water, not just peroxide. Hydrogen peroxide can actually damage the tissue and slow down the healing process. If you're worried about tetanus, you should definitely get a booster shot, but it's not an emergency. You can go to a free clinic or a community health center to get one. But if you notice any signs of infection, like redness, swelling, or pus, then you should definitely see a doctor. Remember, I'm here to help you, but I can't replace professional medical advice.",
